course: dictionary
lesson: 3310
title: Eucalyptus: a tree and an oil
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A eucalyptus is a tall tree from Australia with long, strong-smelling leaves. It is also called a gum tree. Read this: «The koala looks like a teddy bear that sleeps all day.» The sentence goes on to say its only food is eucalyptus leaves, so eucalyptus must be a plant that koalas eat.
explain: Use the words around a new word to find its meaning. «Along Australia's wetter east coast there are rainforests and tall eucalyptus forests full of animals.» The words tall, forests and full of animals tell you that eucalyptus is a kind of tree. Check by swapping in your meaning: tall tree forests full of animals still makes sense.
explain: The same word can mean something you can smell. «Eucalyptus oil» is the oil from the leaves, used in some medicines and sprays. When you see the word oil or spray next to eucalyptus, it is the liquid, not the tree.
fact: A eucalyptus is a tall tree from Australia, also called a gum tree.
fact: Eucalyptus is the oil from the tree's leaves, used in some medicines and sprays.
fact: «The Kangaroo ran through the blue gums (eucalyptus trees)» shows that a blue gum is one kind of eucalyptus tree.
fact: Koalas eat only a few kinds of eucalyptus leaves, and they rest about 18 to 22 hours a day.
fact: In bushfires, the oils from eucalyptus trees can help fires spread fast.
exercise: What is a eucalyptus? | A bright bird with long tail feathers | A kind of desert sand | A small animal that eats grass | *A tall tree from Australia, also called a gum tree
exercise: Another name for a eucalyptus is a what? | An oak | A rose bush | *A gum tree | A pine
exercise: «The koala sleeps for hours because its food, eucalyptus leaves, has little energy.» What is the koala's food? | *Eucalyptus leaves | Grass seeds | Carrots from the garden | Fish from the river
test: «Along Australia's wetter east coast there are rainforests and tall eucalyptus forests.» What does eucalyptus mean in this sentence? | A kind of rain | *A kind of tall tree | A river in Australia | A type of bird
test: What is eucalyptus oil? | Sand from the desert | A kind of bread | *A liquid from the leaves, used in some medicines and sprays | A brown bird from the forest
exam: Which sentence uses eucalyptus to mean the oil? | Ella climbed the eucalyptus and saw the sea | *Ben sprayed eucalyptus in the room to make it smell fresh | The eucalyptus was tall and grey against the sky | The koala was fast asleep under the eucalyptus
